---
/**
 * /test/controller/multi — Multi-Controller Tester
 * Master SEO & Technical Content Optimization
 * Primary keyword: multi controller tester
 */

import ToolLayout from '@layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import MultiController from '@components/tools/controller/MultiController.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Tests', url: '/test/controller' },
  { name: 'Controller Tests', url: '/test/controller' },
  { name: 'Multi-Controller Tester' },
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How do I test multiple controllers simultaneously in the browser?',
    answer: 'Connect up to 4 gamepads via USB or Bluetooth. Press any button on each controller to initialize its Gamepad API slot. The multi-stage visualizer automatically enumerates and displays Player 1, Player 2, Player 3, and Player 4 in real time.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I connect and test mixed controller brands at the same time?',
    answer: 'Yes! You can connect any combination of gamepads—such as a PS5 DualSense on P1, an Xbox Series X controller on P2, a Nintendo Switch Pro on P3, and a fight stick on P4—and test all inputs simultaneously.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why does my controller swap from Player 1 to Player 2 unexpectedly?',
    answer: 'In the W3C Gamepad API, player index slots (0 through 3) are assigned in the chronological order of first button actuation after browser connection. Disconnecting a controller or waking a sleeping Bluetooth device can cause the OS to assign the next available index.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I use this tool to set up 4-player couch multiplayer games?',
    answer: 'Yes. It is ideal for testing hardware before hosting 4-player local co-op and party games like Super Smash Bros. Ultimate, Overcooked 2, Rocket League, Mario Kart, and local fighting game tournament brackets.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why do multiple wireless controllers cause input stutter over Bluetooth?',
    answer: 'Standard motherboard Bluetooth transceivers can become saturated when handling 3 or 4 simultaneous high-frequency wireless gamepad streams. Connecting at least 2 controllers via direct USB cable eliminates packet collisions.',
  }
];
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Multi-Controller Test (4 Gamepads) — Free Online 4-Player Tester | ControllerTesting.com"
  description="Test up to 4 controllers simultaneously online for free. Multi-gamepad diagnostic for PS5, Xbox, Switch, and PC controllers. Check P1–P4 inputs side-by-side."
  keywords="multi controller tester, test 4 controllers at once, multi gamepad test online, test 2 controllers online, couch co op controller tester, gamepad index test"
  toolName="Multi-Controller Test"
  category="Controller Diagnostic"
  categoryUrl="/test/controller"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  faqs={faqs}
>
  {/* ── Tool Interactive Island ── */}
  <Fragment slot="tool">
    <MultiController />
  </Fragment>

  {/* ── Results Slot ── */}
  <Fragment slot="results">
    <div class="results-summary">
      <h2 class="section-title">Multi-Gamepad Port Management Guidelines</h2>
      <p class="results-text">
        All 4 gamepad slots poll simultaneously at 60Hz. Verify that each player slot operates independently:
      </p>
      <div class="results-legend-grid">
        <div class="legend-card legend-pass">
          <strong class="legend-title">Independent Enumeration (Healthy)</strong>
          <p class="legend-text">Each physical controller occupies a dedicated Player index (P1–P4) with zero cross-talk or button mirroring.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="legend-card legend-warning">
          <strong class="legend-title">Slot Jumping / Re-indexing</strong>
          <p class="legend-text">Controllers swap slots upon reconnect. Ensure all controllers are powered on before launching the game.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="legend-card legend-fail">
          <strong class="legend-title">USB Host Saturation (Dropouts)</strong>
          <p class="legend-text">Inputs lag or stutter when all 4 players move sticks simultaneously. Connect through separated USB root host hubs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  {/* ── Export Slot ── */}
  <Fragment slot="export">
    <div class="export-banner">
      <div>
        <h3 class="export-title">Need in-depth diagnostics on a specific gamepad?</h3>
        <p class="export-desc">Launch our dedicated Full Diagnostic Wizard to run 5-step hardware sweeps on any individual controller.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="export-buttons">
        <a href="/test/controller/full-diagnostic" class="btn-primary">Run Full Wizard</a>
        <a href="/test/controller/drift" class="btn-secondary">Check Stick Drift</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  {/* ── Related Tools Slot ── */}
  <Fragment slot="related-tools">
    <a href="/test/controller/full-diagnostic" class="tool-card card-base card-hover">
      <h3 class="tool-name">Full Diagnostic Wizard</h3>
      <p class="tool-desc">Run 5-step hardware checkup.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/test/controller/drift" class="tool-card card-base card-hover">
      <h3 class="tool-name">Stick Drift Tester</h3>
      <p class="tool-desc">Test 0.1% stick drift precision.</p>
    </a>
    <a href="/test/controller/buttons" class="tool-card card-base card-hover">
      <h3 class="tool-name">Button Tester</h3>
      <p class="tool-desc">Test button ghosting and switch chatter.</p>
    </a>
  </Fragment>

  {/* ── SEO Content Slot ── */}
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <h2>Simultaneous Multi-Controller Hardware Architecture</h2>
    <p>
      In local multiplayer gaming, arcade cabinet setups, and competitive tournament staging, running multiple gamepads simultaneously presents unique hardware and driver challenges.
    </p>

    <h3>Gamepad API Index Allocation (P1 through P4)</h3>
    <p>
      The browser Gamepad API maintains an array of connected input devices indexed from <code>navigator.getGamepads()[0]</code> through <code>navigator.getGamepads()[3]</code>.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Standard Mapping (XInput vs. DirectInput):</strong> Windows handles Xbox controllers via XInput (indices 0–3), while PlayStation and Switch controllers communicate via DirectInput/HID. Our diagnostic engine standardizes button mappings across mixed controller protocols.</li>
      <li><strong>USB Host Controller Bandwidth:</strong> Connecting 4 controllers to a single unpowered external USB hub can cause packet collision and dropped polling frames. Distributing connections across separate motherboard USB root hubs ensures consistent 1000Hz/500Hz polling across all players.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Pre-Tournament Controller Verification Protocol</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Connect all 4 tournament gamepads.</li>
      <li>Have all 4 players wiggle their thumbsticks and depress triggers simultaneously to verify zero input dropouts or cross-talk.</li>
      <li>Confirm that each player’s physical controller corresponds to the intended in-game Player 1 through Player 4 slot.</li>
    </ol>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>

<style>
  .results-summary { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .results-text { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  .export-banner { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .export-title { font-size: 1.125rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; }
  .export-desc { font-size: var(--text-small); color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .prose { line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .prose h2, .prose h3 { color: var(--color-text-primary); margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
</style>
